Issue M-1: LossManager applies loss to disabled tranches
Source: https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-02-mezzanine-feb-25th/issues/24
This issue has been acknowledged by the team but won't be fixed at this time.


Summary
Disabled tranches don't receive yield, however they do share loss which is incorrect.


Vulnerability Detail
In yield distribution it skips not enabled tranches:

 for (uint256 i; i < trancheCount; ++i) {
     t = tranches[i];
     trancheTvl = ITranche(t.tranche).totalAssets();
     if (!t.enabled || trancheTvl == 0) continue;
     trancheTvls[i] = trancheTvl;
     totalTvl += trancheTvl;
     // Track the last tranche that actually participates in allocation.
     // Dust will be assigned there to avoid leftover MZUSD on the IssuanceVault.
     lastNonZeroIndex = i;
 }

However there is no such check in loss distribution, it distributes between all tranches. So
users will lose money even when tranche is discontinued.


Impact
LossManager applies loss to disabled tranches. There is no way to remove tranche, so
discontinued tranches will be marked as disabled and will share loss forever.


Code Snippet
https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-02-mezzanine-feb-25th/blob/main/mezzanin
e-sc/contracts/LossManager.sol#L154-L199


Tool Used
Manual Review

 Recommendation
Skip disabled tranches in LossManager._applyLossAcrossOrder()

Issue M-2: NavOracleAutomation.performUpkeep() can
revert wasting funds
Source: https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-02-mezzanine-feb-25th/issues/26


Summary
Chainlink Automation calls checkUpkeep() offchain and executes performUpkeep() when
it returns true. However it doesn't check some cases which cause revert. As a result,
Chainlink will submit reverting transactions which consume funds.


Vulnerability Detail
checkUpkeep() returns true as soon as vetoPeriod has passed.

      function checkUpkeep(
          bytes calldata checkData
      ) external view returns (bool upkeepNeeded, bytes memory performData) {
          checkData;
          if (!hasPendingNav()) return (false, "");
 @>       if (block.timestamp < pendingReadyAt) return (false, "");
          return (true, "");
      }

      function hasPendingNav() public view returns (bool) {
          return pendingReadyAt != 0;
      }

      function performUpkeep(bytes calldata performData) external {
          performData;
          if (!hasPendingNav()) revert NoPendingNav();
          uint256 readyAt = pendingReadyAt;
          if (block.timestamp < readyAt) revert NotReady(readyAt);
          _applyPending();
      }

      function _applyPending() internal {
          bool isYield = pendingIsYield;
          uint256 deltaUSDC = pendingDeltaUSDC;
          uint256 readyAt = pendingReadyAt;

         _clearPending();

         if (isYield) {
             IVault(vault).distributeYield(deltaUSDC);
