Incorrect Version Parsing MEDIUM    OS-SDB-ADV-05

Description

The vulnerability in parseVersion within db is related to the use of strconv.ParseInt with
bitSize set to 32. This limits the parsed integer to the range of an int32 . Since version numbers in
the code’s context should be of type int64 , utilizing strconv.ParseInt with bitSize set to 32
may result in an inability to parse version numbers greater than Int32.Max .

>_ sc/memiavl/db.go    go
func parseVersion(name string) (int64, error) {
if !isSnapshotName(name) {
return 0, fmt.Errorf("invalid snapshot name %s", name)
}

v, err := strconv.ParseInt(name[len(SnapshotPrefix):], 10, 32)
if err != nil {
return 0, fmt.Errorf("snapshot version overflows: %d", err)
}

return v, nil
}

Thus, this restricts the valid version numbers to the range of signed integers ( Int32.Max ), whereas the
version numbers should be treated as unsigned integers to cover the full range up to Uint32.Max .

Remediation

Use strconv.ParseUint with bitSize set to 64 to handle the entire range of Uint32.Max .

